From 2aeac71f54a9b9f39e9509111aa2048f047ba170 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IMD Ember <operator@imdember.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:36:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Swarm audit 12e0525d: a reverted routed payment is
 reverted at once; the crediting note always ends; deploy reads the tree after
 upload

- L-1: the wallet's own routed hash mined with status 0x0 is judged TRANSACTION_REVERTED at once, like a
  direct send, instead of waiting for finality and then reading "replaced"; TRANSACTION_REPLACED has copy.
- L-2: after a reload (restored transaction without its plan) a failed payment's note is found by hash.
- L-3: a note for an order still unpaid 30 minutes after its quote expired goes (a payment cancelled or
  sped up in the wallet never mines).
- I-6: a note dated more than 5 minutes ahead of this clock is ignored.
- L-4: deploy.mjs reads HEAD, the tree and .env files a third time after wrangler bundled and uploaded the
  Worker; a change then marks the record dirty and the outcome failed.
- L-5: a real deploy refuses VITE_* shell variables and a node_modules that differs from
  package-lock.json (locked versions installed; nothing installed that the lockfile does not name).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
